SUMMARY:The Gulf at War: History and Archaeology of Revolutionary West Flo
 rida
DESCRIPTION:UWF's College of Arts\, Social Sciences and Humanities and its
  Archaeology Institute present The Gulf at War: History and Archaeology o
 f Revolutionary West Florida. The talk\, at Voices of Pensacola\, covers 
 the northern Gulf Coast's role in the American Revolution. Pulitzer Prize
  winning historian Dr. Jack E. Davis gives the keynote and moderates a pa
 nel. A reception follows\, with educational displays\, a book signing wit
 h Davis\, and after-hours access to the Pensacola Museum of History's Roa
 d to Revolution exhibit. The reception starts at 5:30 PM and the program 
 at 6:00 PM\, running to 8:30 PM. No admission price is published.\nPrice:
  not published by the venue\, so confirm before you go\nArea: Pensacola\n
 Times: Wednesday 9/23 · Reception 5:30 PM · Program 6:00 PM\nChecked ag
